ison", "start": 91.725, "end": 92.425}]}, {"index": 8, "kind": "prose", "text": "This is the section that separates \"we use a queue\" from \"we understand our queue\":", "start": 92.675, "end": 97.875, "words": [{"text": "This", "start": 92.95, "end": 93.15}, {"text": "is", "start": 93.15, "end": 93.3}, {"text": "the", "start": 93.3, "end": 93.438}, {"text": "section", "start": 93.438, "end": 93.875}, {"text": "that", "start": 93.875, "end": 94.087}, {"text": "separates", "start": 94.087, "end": 94.938}, {"text": "we", "start": 94.938, "end": 95.15}, {"text": "use", "start": 95.15, "end": 95.337}, {"text": "a", "start": 95.337, "end": 95.438}, {"text": "queue", "start": 95.438, "end": 95.8}, {"text": "from", "start": 95.8, "end": 96.2}, {"text": "we", "start": 96.2, "end": 96.375}, {"text": "understand", "start": 96.375, "end": 96.862}, {"text": "our", "start": 96.862, "end": 97.0}, {"text": "queue", "start": 97.0, "end": 97.45}]}, {"index": 9, "kind": "prose", "text": "At-most-once — the message may be lost, but never duplicated. Fast, and fine for metrics or heartbeats where a dropped sample is harmless.", "start": 97.875, "end": 107.0, "words": [{"text": "At", "start": 98.15, "end": 99.213}, {"text": "most", "start": 99.213, "end": 99.213}, {"text": "once", "start": 99.213, "end": 99.213}, {"text": "the", "start": 99.213, "end": 99.3}, {"text": "message", "start": 99.3, "end": 99.7}, {"text": "may", "start": 99.7, "end": 99.838}, {"text": "be", "start": 99.838, "end": 99.975}, {"text": "lost", "start": 99.975, "end": 100.55}, {"text": "but", "start": 100.55, "end": 100.775}, {"text": "never", "start": 100.775, "end": 101.075}, {"text": "duplicated", "start": 101.075, "end": 102.15}, {"text": "Fast", "start": 102.15, "end": 102.85}, {"text": "and", "start": 102.85, "end": 103.062}, {"text": "fine", "start": 103.062, "end": 103.425}, {"text": "for", "start": 103.425, "end": 103.55}, {"text": "metrics", "start": 103.55, "end": 104.062}, {"text": "or", "start": 104.062, "end": 104.225}, {"text": "heartbeats", "start": 104.225, "end": 104.8}, {"text": "where", "start": 104.8, "end": 104.938}, {"text": "a", "start": 104.938, "end": 105.0}, {"text": "dropped", "start": 105.0, "end": 105.412}, {"text": "sample", "start": 105.412, "end": 105.825}, {"text": "is", "start": 105.825, "end": 105.95}, {"text": "harmless", "start": 105.95, "end": 106.75}]}, {"index": 10, "kind": "prose", "text": "At-least-once — the message will arrive, possibly more than once. The workhorse default (SQS standard queues, RabbitMQ with acknowledgments). Your consumers must be idempotent — processing the same message twice must be safe.", "start": 107.0, "end": 122.1, "words": [{"text": "At", "start": 107.275, "end": 108.237}, {"text": "least", "start": 108.237, "end": 108.237}, {"text": "once", "start": 108.237, "end": 108.237}, {"text": "the", "start": 108.237, "end": 108.325}, {"text": "message", "start": 108.325, "end": 108.75}, {"text": "will", "start": 108.75, "end": 108.9}, {"text": "arrive", "start": 108.9, "end": 109.525}, {"text": "possibly", "start": 109.525, "end": 110.175}, {"text": "more", "start": 110.175, "end": 110.4}, {"text": "than", "start": 110.4, "end": 110.525}, {"text": "once", "start": 110.525, "end": 111.3}, {"text": "The", "start": 111.3, "end": 111.575}, {"text": "workhorse", "start": 111.575, "end": 112.075}, {"text": "default", "start": 112.075, "end": 112.713}, {"text": "SQS", "start": 112.713, "end": 113.35}, {"text": "standard", "start": 113.35, "end": 113.812}, {"text": "queues", "start": 113.812, "end": 114.45}, {"text": "RabbitMQ", "start": 114.45, "end": 115.35}, {"text": "with", "start": 115.35, "end": 115.487}, {"text": "acknowledgments", "start": 115.487, "end": 116.625}, {"text": "Your", "start": 116.625, "end": 116.95}, {"text": "consumers", "start": 116.95, "end": 117.575}, {"text": "must", "start": 117.575, "end": 117.825}, {"text": "be", "start": 117.825, "end": 118.013}, {"text": "idempotent", "start": 118.013, "end": 119.0}, {"text": "processing", "start": 119.0, "end": 119.638}, {"text": "the", "start": 119.638, "end": 119.75}, {"text": "same", "start": 119.75, "end": 120.1}, {"text": "message", "start": 120.1, "end": 120.475}, {"text": "twice", "start": 120.475, "end": 120.875}, {"text": "must", "start": 120.875, "end": 121.112}, {"text": "be", "start": 121.112, "end": 121.263}, {"text": "safe", "start": 121.263, "end": 121.875}]}, {"index": 11, "kind": "prose", "text": "Exactly-once — arrives once and only once. Sounds ideal, sounds expensive, and — here's the industry's open secret — is usually at-least-once plus idempotency wearing a trench coat. Kafka offers exactly-once semantics via transactions, but only within Kafka-to-Kafka flows; the moment your consumer calls an external API, you're back to designing for duplicates.", "start": 122.1, "end": 146.325, "words": [{"text": "Exactly", "start": 122.375, "end": 122.9}, {"text": "once", "start": 122.9, "end": 123.512}, {"text": "arrives", "start": 123.512, "end": 124.05}, {"text": "once", "start": 124.05, "end": 124.35}, {"text": "and", "start": 124.35, "end": 124.475}, {"text": "only", "start": 124.475, "end": 124.775}, {"text": "once", "start": 124.775, "end": 125.55}, {"text": "Sounds", "start": 125.55, "end": 126.062}, {"text": "ideal", "start": 126.062, "end": 126.65}, {"text": "sounds", "start": 126.65, "end": 127.087}, {"text": "expensive", "start": 127.087, "end": 128.025}, {"text": "and", "start": 128.025, "end": 128.312}, {"text": "here's", "start": 128.312, "end": 128.662}, {"text": "the", "start": 128.662, "end": 128.775}, {"text": "industry's", "start": 128.775, "end": 129.338}, {"text": "open", "start": 129.338, "end": 129.688}, {"text": "secret", "start": 129.688, "end": 130.45}, {"text": "is", "start": 130.45, "end": 130.688}, {"text": "usually", "start": 130.688, "end": 131.112}, {"text": "at", "start": 131.112, "end": 131.925}, {"text": "least", "start": 131.925, "end": 131.925}, {"text": "once", "start": 131.925, "end": 131.925}, {"text": "plus", "start": 131.925, "end": 132.213}, {"text": "idempotency", "start": 132.213, "end": 133.088}, {"text": "wearing", "start": 133.088, "end": 133.4}, {"text": "a", "start": 133.4, "end": 133.475}, {"text": "trench", "start": 133.475, "end": 133.8}, {"text": "coat", "start": 133.8, "end": 134.575}, {"text": "Kafka", "start": 134.575, "end": 135.237}, {"text": "offers", "start": 135.237, "end": 135.675}, {"text": "exactly", "start": 135.675, "end": 136.475}, {"text": "once", "start": 136.475, "end": 136.475}, {"text": "semantics", "start": 136.475, "end": 137.1}, {"text": "via", "start": 137.1, "end": 137.325}, {"text": "transactions", "start": 137.325, "end": 138.375}, {"text": "but", "start": 138.375, "end": 138.6}, {"text": "only", "start": 138.6, "end": 138.9}, {"text": "within", "start": 138.9, "end": 139.188}, {"text": "Kafka", "start": 139.188, "end": 140.062}, {"text": "to", "start": 140.062, "end": 140.062}, {"text": "Kafka", "start": 140.062, "end": 140.062}, {"text": "flows", "start": 140.062, "end": 140.825}, {"text": "the", "start": 140.825, "end": 141.025}, {"text": "moment", "start": 141.025, "end": 141.312}, {"text": "your", "start": 141.312, "end": 141.425}, {"text": "consumer", "start": 141.425, "end": 141.987}, {"text": "calls", "start": 141.987, "end": 142.375}, {"text": "an", "start": 142.375, "end": 142.475}, {"text": "external", "start": 142.475, "end": 143.025}, {"text": "API", "start": 143.025, "end": 143.875}, {"text": "you're", "start": 143.875, "end": 144.175}, {"text": "back", "start": 144.175, "end": 144.475}, {"text": "to", "start": 144.475, "end": 144.575}, {"text": "designing", "start": 144.575, "end": 145.075}, {"text": "for", "start": 145.075, "end": 145.2}, {"text": "duplicates", "start": 145.2, "end": 146.075}]}, {"index": 12, "kind": "prose", "text": "The practical rule: assume at-least-once, make your handlers idempotent (dedupe keys, upserts instead of inserts), and sleep well.", "st